{"uid":"3e10e228543fb5a7","name":"test_clicking_list_detail_list_detail_via_real_links_discards_a_stale_response","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_refresh_loop_clicks#test_clicking_list_detail_list_detail_via_real_links_discards_a_stale_response","historyId":"364ab8420414f0b326133d6a64dead64","time":{"start":1791883203354,"stop":1791883216624,"duration":13270},"description":"Click list -> run-a's detail -> back to the list -> run-b's detail,\n    entirely through the page's own rendered `<a>` links. Targets the\n    `myGen !== renderGeneration || seq !== loadSeq` guard inside\n    `renderRunDetail`'s `load()`: several of the sub-renders it drives\n    (`renderTasks(document.getElementById(\"task-box\"), ...)` among them)\n    look their target element up fresh by id, and every `renderRunDetail`\n    call reuses the same ids -- so a stale response for run-a landing after\n    run-b's detail view has already replaced the DOM does not write into a\n    detached node, it writes into *run-b's own live element*. Reverting\n    either guard (or `loadSeq` itself) makes run-a's marker task reappear in\n    run-b's live task list once run-a's delayed response lands, exactly as\n    in `tests/test_browser_hub_refresh_loop.py`'s function-call-driven\n    version of this same defect -- this test pins the identical mechanism\n    reached by real navigation through the list in between, instead.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Click list -&gt; run-a's detail -&gt; back to the list -&gt; run-b's detail,<br />\nentirely through the page's own rendered <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> links. Targets the<br />\n<code>myGen !== renderGeneration || seq !== loadSeq</code> guard inside<br />\n<code>renderRunDetail</code>'s <code>load()</code>: several of the sub-renders it drives<br />\n(<code>renderTasks(document.getElementById(&quot;task-box&quot;), ...)</code> among them)<br />\nlook their target element up fresh by id, and every <code>renderRunDetail</code><br />\ncall reuses the same ids -- so a stale response for run-a landing after<br />\nrun-b's detail view has already replaced the DOM does not write into a<br />\ndetached node, it writes into <em>run-b's own live element</em>. Reverting<br />\neither guard (or <code>loadSeq</code> itself) makes run-a's marker task reappear in<br />\nrun-b's live task list once run-a's delayed response lands, exactly as<br />\nin <code>tests/test_browser_hub_refresh_loop.py</code>'s function-call-driven<br />\nversion of this same defect -- this test pins the identical mechanism<br />\nreached by real navigation through the list in between, instead.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791882060905,"stop":1791882060905,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791882060905,"stop":1791882060905,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791883203351,"stop":1791883203351,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791883203351,"stop":1791883203352,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791883203352,"stop":1791883203352,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDispla